<idea-plugin require-restart="true">
    <id>jp.titze.helix</id>
    <name>Helix Keymap (T68k)</name>
    <vendor url="https://github.com/Toshi68k">Thorsten Titze</vendor>

    <description><![CDATA[
<p>
  <b>Helix Keymap</b> brings the modern, selection-first modal editing paradigm of the 
  <a href="https://helix-editor.com">Helix editor</a> directly into JetBrains IDEs. 
  Rather than layering fragile vim emulations or static keymaps, this plugin deeply integrates 
  authentic Helix workflows with IntelliJ's native <code>CaretModel</code>, <code>SelectionModel</code>, 
  PSI/AST structure, and <code>ActionManager</code>.
</p>

<div style="background-color: #fff9db; border: 1px solid #f59f00; padding: 10px 14px; margin-bottom: 14px; color: #212529;">
  <b>Beta Notice:</b> I have been using this plugin for real work for several weeks; however, it is considered <b>beta</b> and might still contain bugs or incorrect behavior. Feedback and issue reports are warmly welcomed on <a href="https://github.com/Toshi68k/t68k-intellij-helix/issues">GitHub</a>, but please don't flood me with AI slop!
</div>

<h3>The Selection-First Paradigm</h3>
<p>
  Traditional modal editors rely on the <i>verb → object</i> pattern (such as <code>d3w</code>), 
  forcing you to guess text boundaries before acting. Helix inverts this into <b>selection → action</b>: 
  every motion creates or manipulates a visible selection, providing instant visual feedback before executing 
  a delete, change, or yank.
</p>

<h3>Key Features</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    <b>Interactive Which-Key Popups:</b> 
    Pressing <kbd>Space</kbd> (with dedicated refactor <code>space m</code>, test <code>space t</code>, VCS <code>space v</code>, and Harpoon <code>space H</code> submenus), <code>g</code>, <code>m</code>, <code>[</code>, <code>]</code>, <code>z</code>, <code>Z</code>, <code>Ctrl+w</code>, or <code>"</code> reveals an instant visual chord menu in authentic <code>snake_case</code>. Live register contents preview on <code>"</code> and <kbd>Ctrl+r</kbd>. Press <kbd>Tab</kbd> to inspect underlying IntelliJ Action IDs in real time, or bypass the popup entirely with rapid muscle memory.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Harpoon-Style Quick Slots &amp; Bookmarks Integration:</b> 
    Deterministic 2-keystroke jumps to pinned working slots (<code>space + 1..5</code>), dynamic shift tracking via <code>RangeMarker</code>, and an interactive floating card UI (<code>space + H H</code> / <code>:harpoon</code>) with code snippet previews, pinning (<code>a</code>), unpinning (<code>d</code>), and live slot reordering (<kbd>Shift+J</kbd>/<kbd>Shift+K</kbd>). Seamlessly bridges IntelliJ native bookmarks (<code>:bookmarks</code>, <code>:bookmark-toggle</code>).
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Dedicated Test &amp; VCS Leader Keymaps:</b> 
    Fast TDD testing workflow via <code>space + t</code> (run, debug, rerun, test file, coverage) and comprehensive Git/VCS operations via <code>space + v</code> (diff, blame, status, commit, push, pull, log, and merge conflict navigation).
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Tool Windows Modal Navigation (Experimental):</b> 
    Modal Helix keyboard navigation (<code>j</code>/<code>k</code>, <code>h</code>/<code>l</code>, <code>gg</code>/<code>ge</code>, <code>Ctrl+d</code>/<code>Ctrl+u</code>, native speed search <code>/</code>, <code>n</code>/<code>N</code>) across Project view, Git log, Structure, Problems, and tool window trees, lists, and tables.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Configurable Keymaps &amp; Editor Options (<code>config.toml</code> / <code>intellij.toml</code>):</b> 
    Authentic Helix key rebinding and <code>[editor]</code> table configuration via <code>~/.config/helix/intellij.toml</code> (or fallback <code>config.toml</code>) with a zero-dependency pure Kotlin TOML parser. Supports multi-command macros, direct IntelliJ actions (<code>:action &lt;ActionId&gt;</code>), key unbinding (<code>"no_op"</code>), 3-way CLI fallback policy, and automatic VFS live reloading on save without restarting the IDE.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Visual Keymap Customizer &amp; Conflict Detection:</b> 
    Interactive Keybindings Explorer in Settings with chord filters, real-time search, shortcut recording (<i>Find by Shortcut...</i>), provenance badges, and trie prefix conflict/shadowing diagnostics. Add, edit, reset, or disable shortcuts via a modal dialog with safe, non-destructive TOML persistence.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Native Multi-Caret &amp; Piece-Wise Registers:</b> 
    Add cursors vertically (<code>Alt+C</code> / <code>C</code>), split on regex patterns or newlines (<code>s</code>, <code>S</code>, <code>Alt+s</code>), filter selections (<code>K</code>, <code>Alt+K</code>), select occurrences (<code>add_selection_next</code> / <code>select_all_occurrences</code>), and align into columns (<code>&amp;</code>). Supports named (<code>"a</code>–<code>"z</code>), clipboard (<code>"+</code>), black hole (<code>"_</code>), selection-index (<code>"#</code>), and last insert (<code>".</code>) registers with authentic 1:1 piece-wise multi-caret pasting.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Helix Inline Macros (<code>@</code> Syntax) &amp; Macro Picker:</b> 
    Full support for Helix's canonical <code>@...</code> inline macro playback syntax in key bindings (e.g. <code>"\"" = "@f\"lmi\""</code>), keystroke tokenization with special keys (<code>&lt;ret&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;esc&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;A-o&gt;</code>), and an interactive macro picker popup (<code>:macros</code>) with previews and fuzzy search.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Surround &amp; PSI Textobjects (<code>m</code> menu):</b> 
    Add, replace, and delete surround delimiters (<code>ms</code>, <code>mr</code>, <code>md</code>) and match brackets (<code>mm</code>). Select inside and around structural elements including functions (<code>maf</code>), classes (<code>mat</code>), arguments (<code>maa</code>), indent blocks (<code>mii</code>), XML tags (<code>max</code>), tests (<code>maT</code>), and VCS hunks (<code>mag</code>).
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>AST-Aware &amp; Unimpaired Navigation:</b> 
    Expand/shrink selection by syntax tree scope (<code>Alt+o</code> / <code>Alt+i</code>), navigate AST sibling elements (<code>Alt+p</code> / <code>Alt+n</code>), move to parent boundaries (<code>Alt+b</code> / <code>Alt+e</code>), or jump between functions, diagnostics, comments, VCS changes, paragraphs, and XML elements via <code>[</code> and <code>]</code> chords.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Helix Gutter Line Numbers &amp; Visual Modes:</b> 
    Full Helix line number support: <code>Absolute</code>, <code>Relative</code>, <code>Hybrid</code> (Helix default), <code>Pure-Relative</code>, and <code>Smart</code> (relative in Normal/Select mode with automatic absolute fallback in Insert mode). Mode-colored status bar pills (Indigo Normal, Emerald Insert, Magenta Select), dynamic editor cursor tinting (<code>cursor-tint = true</code>), and flash-on-yank feedback.
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Helix Command Palette &amp; Shell Filters (<code>:</code>):</b> 
    Fast fuzzy completion for buffer actions, shell piping (<code>|</code>, <code>!</code>, <code>$</code>), numeric sorting (<code>:sort -n</code>), window &amp; scratch splits (<code>Ctrl+w n s</code> / <code>n v</code>), view maximization (<code>:maximize-view</code>), tab management (<code>:close-to-right</code>, <code>:close-unmodified</code>, <code>:reopen-closed-tab</code>), Git commands (<code>:branches</code>, <code>:blame</code>, <code>:diff</code>, <code>:commit</code>), DAP debugging, and runtime option controls (<code>:set-option</code>, <code>:toggle-option</code> for soft-wrap, inlay hints, whitespace, etc.).
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>Space Leader Highlights</h3>
<ul>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>1..5</code></b> → Instant jump to Harpoon quick slot 1–5</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>H</code></b> → Harpoon quick slot submenu &amp; interactive card picker</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>f</code> / <code>b</code></b> → File picker (<code>GotoFile</code>) / Buffer switcher (<code>RecentFiles</code>)</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>F</code></b> → File picker in current directory (<code>HelixDirectoryFilePickerPopup</code>)</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>B</code></b> → Recent Locations with visual code snippet previews (<code>RecentLocations</code>)</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>m</code></b> → Refactor submenu (extract variable/method/constant, inline, rename, change signature, safe delete, generate code, pull up / push down)</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>t</code></b> → Test runner submenu (run, debug, rerun, coverage, run file, run all)</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>v</code></b> → Version control &amp; Git submenu (diff, blame, status, commit, push, pull, log, conflicts)</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>/</code></b> → Project-wide text search (<code>FindInPath</code>)</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>s</code> / <code>S</code></b> → Document structure &amp; workspace symbol search</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>a</code> / <code>r</code></b> → Code actions (<kbd>Alt+Enter</kbd>) &amp; symbol rename</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>d</code> / <code>D</code></b> → Diagnostic inspection &amp; Problems tool window</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>j</code></b> → Interactive Jumplist picker popup</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>w</code> / <code>W</code></b> → Window &amp; split layout management / Tool Window Switcher</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>G</code></b> → Interactive DAP debugging menu (breakpoints, stepping, eval)</li>
  <li><b><kbd>Space</kbd> + <code>k</code> / <code>?</code></b> → Documentation hover &amp; command search</li>
</ul>

<h3>Configuration &amp; Settings Hierarchy</h3>
<p>
  Configure all plugin behavior under <b>Settings → Tools → Helix Keymap</b>:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Helix Keymap:</b> Core preferences across 3 tabs (<i>General &amp; Scope</i>, <i>Appearance &amp; UI</i>, and <i>Behavior &amp; Navigation</i>).</li>
  <li><b>Keybindings (sub-page):</b> Dedicated visual keymap browser, keystroke recorder, conflict warnings, custom binding editor, and platform Ctrl key routing.</li>
  <li><b>Configuration (sub-page):</b> Dedicated <code>intellij.toml</code> path management, CLI conflict guards, and live reload diagnostics.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Documentation &amp; Support</h3>
<p>
  Source code, documentation, and issue tracker:
  <a href="https://github.com/Toshi68k/t68k-intellij-helix">GitHub Repository</a> |
  <a href="https://github.com/Toshi68k/t68k-intellij-helix/issues">Issue Tracker</a>
</p>
    ]]></description>

    <depends>com.intellij.modules.platform</depends>
    <!--suppress PluginXmlValidity -->
    <incompatible-with>IdeaVIM</incompatible-with>

    <resource-bundle>messages.HelixBundle</resource-bundle>

    <extensions defaultExtensionNs="com.intellij">
        <postStartupActivity implementation="jp.titze.intellij.helix.editor.HelixStartupActivity"/>
        <editorFactoryListener implementation="jp.titze.intellij.helix.editor.HelixEditorListener"/>
        <statusBarWidgetFactory implementation="jp.titze.intellij.helix.ui.HelixStatusBarWidgetFactory"
                                id="jp.titze.intellij.helix.status"/>
        <applicationConfigurable parentId="tools"
                                 instance="jp.titze.intellij.helix.settings.HelixConfigurable"
                                 id="jp.titze.intellij.helix.settings"
                                 key="settings.displayName"/>
        <applicationConfigurable parentId="jp.titze.intellij.helix.settings"
                                 instance="jp.titze.intellij.helix.settings.HelixKeybindingsConfigurable"
                                 id="jp.titze.intellij.helix.settings.keybindings"
                                 key="settings.keybindings.displayName"/>
        <applicationConfigurable parentId="jp.titze.intellij.helix.settings"
                                 instance="jp.titze.intellij.helix.settings.HelixConfigFileConfigurable"
                                 id="jp.titze.intellij.helix.settings.config"
                                 key="settings.config.displayName"/>
    </extensions>

    <applicationListeners>
        <listener class="jp.titze.intellij.helix.config.HelixConfigWatcher"
                  topic="com.intellij.openapi.vfs.newvfs.BulkFileListener"/>
    </applicationListeners>

    <projectListeners>
        <listener class="jp.titze.intellij.helix.editor.HelixFileEditorListener"
                  topic="com.intellij.openapi.fileEditor.FileEditorManagerListener"/>
    </projectListeners>

